judge_checks.pipgraft:
Sortie pip dynamics at a trimmed radius of 240 PvE / 190 Arena:
- parked pip at 100/150/200 px: 0.30 s 53 deg, 0.52 s 118 deg, 0.67 s 108 deg;
- fly-by width 465 px (1.95x today; Arcade as specced gives 471);
- Arena 380 px (1.60x);
- Magnet L5 2.10x base;
- Tractor 1164 px.
At Sortie's own 320/240: 631 px (2.65x).

judge_checks.powergraft:
Arcade Artificer, Phaser + E-hold Ray:
- at 170/s it never browns out in 30 s;
- at 200/s the first brownout is at 13.8 s;
- at 210/s it is at 11.7 s.
Polarize sustain alone never browns out in 60 s at 200 or 240/s (under 300 dps fire: 23.5 s / 14.8 s). A price change alone therefore cannot end it; a duration cap is needed.

notes.d:
Best persistence design: no stored power, perkRule, and a +-10% share gate. It also has the most counterplay holes:
- the only EMP that is inescapable inside its radius;
- three lethal EMP-then-ult chains;
- a Hyperlance spool that can track;
- the Wrecking Run re-hit loop;
- a Drone Carrier that shooting the drones cannot answer;
- Strafe Dodge beats every signature perk;
- Ram + Salvo one-shots the Arcanist (420 integrity).

No lethal two-ult chain: the best leaves the Arcanist at 0/140. Event Horizon's pull is divided by capitalMass and adds gravity shear; bombs deal 300. Holes:
- Ram + Salvo one-shots (a single knob fixes it);
- the Gravity Well trap (shared by all kits);
- Q in brownout;
- Overdrive is dominated as an escape;
- the Flight Log puts non-cosmetic data in the profile, and guests cannot earn perks.

notes.g:
Keeps the InputState / SkillSlot wire names and the 39 B ship record; 3 ult systems plus modifiers; 5 perks. Risks:
- PROFILE_VERSION 2 (removed by G7);
- the E tap/hold grammar;
- the capital cooldown moving to utilityReadyTick (shared by all kits).

notes.a:
Slots and pad are right, but:
- E and Q are 3-per-class loadout picks (the owner asked for one E per class, with path variants);
- persistent unlocks extend past perks to E and Q;
- the Arcanist coast-brake nerf (1800 -> 1100) works against owner requirement 8.

notes.d:
The most complete fairness framework: F1-F7, Open Loadout in Arena, CC diminishing returns, the pull cap, RAM_VS_SHIP. It is also the only kit that passes the burst rule. But it has the largest attack surface:
- a lethal EMP -> Carpet Bomb chain;
- a Hyperlance charge that can track;
- a Drone Carrier that shooting the drones cannot answer;
- an uncapped Rampage;
- a Mortar that ignores walls;
- a Jump through walls;
- mastery-gated E and Q in Warzone and Dungeon.

why:
Arcade has the highest total: 52/70, against Hero 42 and Sortie 35. It wins or ties 5 of the 7 criteria:
- the most exact match to the owner's Overwatch layout;
- the only kit that honours 'keep it simple and frantic';
- the safest simulated numbers (no lethal two-ult chain, lowest dungeon ult share);
- the smallest contract churn, because it keeps the wire names.
Its weaknesses are all knob-level or graftable: the Ram one-shot, the FULL STOP trap, the Gravity Well trap, the pip model and the Flight Log schema bump.

required_fixes.fix:
Gravity Well:
- hostile-ship pull = min(wellPull, 300) / capitalMass(n);
- all hostile pulls on one ship sum to at most SHIP_PULL_CAP 600;
- 1 well alive per Arcanist, a new one replacing the old;
- Deep Well (voi_horizon) +2 s -> +1 s.

Pin the E tap/hold grammar for the Artificer and the Foundry:
- if E is released before 12 ticks, Repair Pulse (Foundry: Repair Bay) fires on release;
- a hold that reaches 12 ticks starts the Ray and does not fire the Pulse;
- if the tap skill is on cooldown, the Ray starts on press.
Bots set this directly. The predictor applies Pulse's x1.3 boost from the release tick.

grafts.what:
Pip dynamics at Arcade's economy, using Sortie's two-zone well:
- linear accel A(1-u)+320;
- swirl 1.1a, fading over 1.1 s;
- tangential damping (2+4t)/s;
- relative cap 700;
- capture pad 60, collect pad 10.
Base radius 240 PvE / 190 Arena, x sqrt(r/18); capital x(1+0.12n); A x sqrt(capitalMass). Keep Arcade's strongest-pull contest with 1.25x hysteresis, its Tractor Field / Vacuum numbers and its Magnet rework.

Derive persistent perk unlocks from the EXISTING Profile.stats with a pure perkUnlocked(stats, perk, class) in data/perks.ts. Drop Arcade's Flight Log: PROFILE_VERSION stays 1 and ARCHITECTURE §3c is untouched. Unlocks:
- starters: the class home perk and Strafe Dodge;
- the other two home perks: stats.matches >= 5;
- Hyperspace Jump: byType.dungeon.matches >= 3, or matches >= 20.
Arcade's in-match Perk cards (levels 5 and 10) stay as the trial path.

Tells:
- Ion Storm's first arc lands 0.5 s after the disc;
- every ult cast sends a positional ult-call sound to clients in range;
- ships inside the ult's reach get a red edge pointer.

Docked ultimates:
- a docked Arcanist throws Ion Storm from its dome;
- a docked Artificer's Overload centres on its host;
- a docked Juggernaut's Event Horizon undocks it first.

not_grafted:
Hero:
- the Repair Ray on RMB (it breaks the owner's RMB list, and Phaser + Ray breaks even forever);
- the pre-path ult cap that queues the path fork (not needed for a class-bound ult);
- ShipView.ultFrac in the ship record (G4 is cheaper).

Sortie:
- the 3 E x 3 Q loadout variants, Class Mastery, Pilot Rank and PROFILE_VERSION 2 (the owner asked for one E per class and for simple and frantic);
- the InputState / ShipStats renames (44 files);
- the Arcanist coast-brake nerf 1800 -> 1100 (owner requirement 8);
- the Tractor maneuver perk (a persistent XP-pull option);
- Mortar over walls and Jump through walls.
